1 NOTE
2 CONT Mark Gordon Clauson, 21, Spring Grove, died Sunday July 2nd, 1972 at Luthean Hospital, La Crosse, WI.  He had been there since June 11th when the motorcycle he was driving collided with a car on Highway 44 east of Spring Grove.  T
2 CONC he son of Carlton and Valborg Peterson Clauson, he was born at Spring Grove, February 21, 1951.  He was a 1969 graducate of Spring Grove High School and attended Winona State College two years.  He was a member of Trinity Lutheran
2 CONC  Church of Spring Grove.
2 CONT Survivors are:L  his parents; three brothers, Truman, Rochester, MN and Neil and Timothy at home; four sisters, Mrs. Lloyd (Elizabeth) Cuttings, Millville, MNl; Kathleen, Karen and Mary at home and his paternal grandfather, George
2 CONC  M. Peterson, Spring Grove.
2 CONT Funeral services were held at 11 a.m. Wednesday, July 5th at Trinity Lutheran Church, the Rev. Kenneth G. Knutson and Rev. Jess W. Thompson officiated.  Burial was in the church cemetery.  Honorary pallbears were:  Gordon Myhre, D
2 CONC ale Roble, David Myrah, Bill Buxengard, Bruce Olson, John Scheevel, Duane Oakes, Don Solberg, Rick Dosser, Mark Kumpf, Robert Hillman and Don Wendel.
2 CONT Casket bearers were:  Curtis Peterson, Gregory Peterson, Duane St. Mary, Tony Elton, Gary Wilhelmson and Dennis Bergrud.
